The shape every other JSON config invites, and the one the daemon drops the
WHOLE file on. Two of the three SDKs used to accept it, so an author's own tests
passed on a file the user's machine never loads.

E6 is the ONLY id here, deliberately. A file that does not parse has no
`listing.name` in it either, and E10 would be true — but piling "your en.json is
missing the two reserved keys" on top of "your en.json was dropped entirely"
sends the author to fix the wrong thing. The rules that need a loaded `en.json`
all stand down when there is not one.
